---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
const controls=[['Your question','Enter one question between 4 and 120 characters. URLs, files, line breaks, and extra context are not accepted.'],['Human check','Cloudflare Turnstile checks that the request is not automated before any model call is made.'],['Personal daily limit','One anonymous visitor can run the tool twice in 24 hours. We use protected identifiers for this limit and do not store the raw IP address.'],['Site-wide daily limit','The whole site can make no more than 40 runs per UTC day. Each accepted request reserves up to €0.02 before it starts.'],['Monthly cost limit','The tool pauses at a €25 monthly warning limit and cannot go beyond the €30 hard limit, including requests that arrive at the same time.'],['One model call','Each run uses one approved gpt-5.4-nano call, up to 700 output tokens, with a 12-second timeout and no automatic retry.'],['What you receive','The result must contain 4–8 branches. Each branch includes a question, likely intent, reason, useful source type, and an assumption to check.'],['What we keep','ai-fanout.com does not store the raw question or raw model answer. It keeps only protected usage identifiers, versions, token counts, cost, timing, and a general status.']];
---
<BaseLayout title="How the free AI query fanout tool works" canonicalPath="/methodology" description="See what the free fanout tool accepts, what it returns, how it protects privacy and costs, and what its suggestions cannot prove.">
<header class="page-head"><h1>How the free tool works</h1><div class="page-head-copy"><p>One short question goes in. A small set of follow-up questions comes out, with enough detail to check every suggestion.</p><p class="meta-line">Tool 1.0.0 · method 1.0 · owner Matthias Ramahi</p></div></header>
<div class="document-layout"><aside class="document-aside"><dl><div><dt>Availability</dt><dd>Not open yet</dd></div><div><dt>Model</dt><dd>gpt-5.4-nano</dd></div><div><dt>Maximum answer</dt><dd>700 tokens</dd></div><div><dt>Time limit</dt><dd>12 seconds</dd></div></dl></aside><article class="document-body"><h2>What the tool does</h2><p class="document-intro">It suggests useful ways to break one broad question into smaller questions. The suggestions come from this tool's own planning call. They are not recovered Google searches, ChatGPT subqueries, private retrieval data, system prompts, or hidden reasoning.</p><ol class="controls">{controls.map(([title,copy],index)=><li><span>{String(index+1).padStart(2,'0')}</span><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{copy}</p></div></li>)}</ol><section><h2>How to use the result</h2><p>Treat every branch as a suggestion to review. Remove repeated ideas, check the available evidence, and look at what your site already covers. A branch may lead to a new page, a section on an existing page, more research, or no action.</p></section><section><h2>Who is responsible</h2><p>Matthias Ramahi runs the site. He is responsible for version changes, corrections, reviewer status, and the monthly cost limit. Results are not independently reviewed by default. Any published example must state its date, exact input, model, tool version, review status, and cost boundary.</p></section><section><h2>What the tool cannot tell you</h2><p>The model can miss an important question, repeat an idea, make a weak assumption, or phrase something poorly. The result is not search-volume data, a ranking forecast, a provider benchmark, or proof that another system followed the same path.</p></section><p><a href="/research/methodology">See how the separate answer-comparison tool is documented</a>.</p></article></div>
</BaseLayout>
<style>.document-body>h2{margin:0;font:720 clamp(3rem,6vw,6rem)/.92 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.06em}.controls{margin:3rem 0 5rem;padding:0;border-top:1px solid var(--rule);list-style:none}.controls li{display:grid;grid-template-columns:4rem 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:1.3rem 0;border-bottom:1px solid var(--fine-rule)}.controls li>span{color:var(--source);font:1rem/1 var(--font-display)}.controls h3{margin:0;font-size:1rem}.controls p,.document-body section p{max-width:65ch;color:var(--muted);line-height:1.65}.document-body section{margin-top:4rem;padding-top:1.5rem;border-top:1px solid var(--rule)}.document-body section h2{font:700 clamp(2rem,4vw,3.6rem)/1 var(--font-display);letter-spacing:-.045em}</style>
